  "title": "Kievan Rus'",
  "summary": "Kievan Rus' was a medieval federation centred on Kyiv, in parts of modern Belarus, Ukraine and Russia. It dates from the mid-9th century, when the Rurik dynasty began. Vladimir the Great converted the region to Christianity, with his baptism dated to 988. Its wealth rested partly on trade with Baltic merchants. The Mongol invasions of 1237–1240 destroyed it, breaking the region into pieces that developed separately.",
